ent. DiamondRock Hospitality Company was established on May 26 2004 and is based in Bethesda, United States.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey John Donnelly C.F.A. | CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 35 people. Revenue per employee of $32.0M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers. Each employee generates $4.6M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $212K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Diamondrock Hospitality Company is a mid-cap real estate business with a $3.0B market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $162M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.40\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 8% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5222929936305737},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"DiamondRock Hospitality (DRH) Posted Stronger Results, Is The Valuation Upside Already Priced In?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nasdaq-drh/diamondrock-hospitality/news/diamondrock-hospitality-drh-posted-stronger-results-is-the-v","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794115918.303,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.914,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What DiamondRock Hospitality (DRH) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/what-diamondrock-hospitality-drh-said-on-its-q3-earnings-call.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793888127.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.7,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"DiamondR